    "summary": "Man&#039;s bag: resembling a shoulder bag: composed of seven hand woven narrow strips hand sewn together selvedge to selvedge. Plain weave: bleached white and dyed green warps: bleached white wefts. This combination of warps and wefts is used to create narrow strips with a single central warp stripe in green. The cut ends of the bad have been hemmed using hand stitch. Inside the bag are visible the remains of the fringe of the original narrow strip textile before it was made into a bag.",
